meta:
  origin:
    producer: World Trade Organization
    title: 'Evolution of trade under the WTO: handy statistics'
    description: |-
      The World Trade Organization (WTO) is the international organization that sets the rules for trade between countries.

      This file gives the volume of world merchandise trade each year since 1950, both as annual growth and as an index with 1950 = 100. The WTO measures trade as the average of exports and imports, leaving out significant re-exports and imports for re-export. Volumes are adjusted for changes in prices.
    citation_full: |-
      World Trade Organization. Evolution of trade under the WTO: handy statistics. Retrieved from https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/evolution_trade_wto_e.htm (Accessed: 22 October 2026).
    url_main: https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/evolution_trade_wto_e.htm
    url_download: https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/world_trade_growth.xlsx
    date_accessed: '2026-10-22'
    # NOTE: The WTO replaces this file in place, without a version label, when it publishes its trade statistics
    # (March–April) and its Global Trade Outlook update (October). The page states no release date: this is the file's HTTP
    # Last-Modified header, which matches the WTO's October 2026 outlook release. Compare the md5 to detect a new file.
    date_published: '2026-10-08'
